# H8: hand the cards back. The LAST card job of the window, and it runs even when a stop job halted the window and after a stall or a hang, which can
# leave all four cards hung: the status of every board and the all-four reset. It decides nothing about WHAT is placed; the driver does, by the GO rule
# in ORDER.txt, in this order after H8: (1) the platform's fabric re-measure on the base image that has the mesh descriptor (it must pass before any
# placement); (2) the :latest decision: GO moves it to the thin layer image built on tp4-serve-8 (publish lane, a dry run first, then apply; the rig
# daemon's local :latest is checked to be the new image), NO-GO leaves it on today's production thin layer and the driver confirms that it and the
# local tag are unchanged; (3) the topology tick; (4) A9 (agentstart: the agent comes back AFTER the :latest decision, because a warm placement
# re-dispatches the moment the agent can); (5) the owner's /deploy with release_first, polled to succeeded.
# WHAT IS PLACED: on GO the eight-seat image (its default c2-packed-tp4-8, session cap 8); on NO-GO TODAY'S PRODUCTION RECIPE (the image and profile
# c2-packed-tp4 that served before). NEVER a gate arm (not c2-packed-tp4-8-gate, -time-gate or -diag-strace, not any gate-only profile) and never
# c2-packed-tp4-8 by an environment variable: an eight-seat placement exists only as the baked default of the shipped image.
# Pass: all four boards enumerate after the reset, the fabric re-measure passes, /v1/models answers with the served name and a chat completes. On GO the
# engine log shows profile c2-packed-tp4-8 and the metrics show thatch_serving_session_cap 8; on NO-GO profile c2-packed-tp4 and cap 4. If the reset does
# not heal a board after a stall, production stays down until it does.
# Duration (estimate): 15 min. Stop rule: any failure stops the window (the placement steps are the driver's).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8 SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8 is the SHIPPING image: the base SB8 builds
# from this branch with the eight-seat profile baked in as its serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its
# seat count (ENV THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP). Every job serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still
# names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default. A commit that changes a file the image carries needs a new SB8 build and a
# new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8
